A||||6||88/2.8||Cold Air Intake/flowmaster exhaust||||6||
Z||000000||88/2.8||05-17-2001||10:14 AM||||I was thinking of putting cold air intake on my car(probably from cwestco) and also a flowmaster and free flow cat. how much of a hp gain would i have?? Would it make alot of difference???||||reg||6
Z||000001||msweldon||05-17-2001||12:17 PM||||Not much, the fiero intake and exhaust on the 2.8's are about as good as it gets.  You could see some improvements with ported stock exhaust manifolds or a pair of custom ones from the fiero store.  I'd recommend going with the ported stock, much cheaper than custom headers.<P>mw||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||05-17-2001||12:20 PM||||I have a Flowie and low restriction cat (sometimes) an a K&N.  I doubt I'm adding any HP, but the old Ass-O-Meter tells me my throttle response seems quicker. Plus it sounds NASTY!||||reg||1
Z||000003||WKDFIRO||05-17-2001||12:34 PM||||I would have to disagree with the notion that the intake and exhaust are as good as it gets. <P>A great majority of people including myself have reported acceleration improvment by just removing the water trap/intake muffler. And many in my club including myself can go on about the benefits of having a 2.5 inch exhaust with the flowmaster for improved performance and sound. Those who have headers love them. Those of us who have ported exhaust manifolds still *****  pretty loudly when they crack...<P>The actual numbers for improvement are still being debated. I there is someone with actual dyno numbers but are not sure.<P>Performance will improve. But don't expect 13 second 1/4 times!<P>(WOOOHOOOOO   800th post!!!!!)<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 05-17-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000004||FieroLisa||05-17-2001||12:39 PM||||I agree with stimpy's ass-o-meter! My GT seems a little quicker at higher RPMs with the cold air intake. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||fyerstarter||05-17-2001||01:07 PM||||Horsepower wise probably maybe 5 hp if your lucky. But my ass-ometer noticed a pretty big improvement  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Funny thing is when I just removed the waterfilter I noticed no improvement at all. But when I went full on intake there was a noticeable difference. Basically you'll spin up quicker and lose some torque. Sorta like a Honda  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fyerstarter.f2s.com/fiero_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||05-17-2001||01:42 PM||||I have a mass air flow meter on my 3800SC and I can flow 190 gm/s of air with the stock V6 box and filter. A K&N raised that to about 200. <P>The engine is capable of about 240 gms with my mods. The 2.8L would be lucky to hit about 150 gms so I don't believe the stock intake is restrictive for the 2.8L engine.<P><BR>On little trick I've used is to connect a vacuum hose on a tube stuck in the TB hose from the filter can. Connect a MAP to it. Get the ground and +5V from the TPS. Connect the output to a voltmeter. If there is a flow restriction, the MAP will see some vacuum forming since the filter can't supply all of the air the engine is trying to suck in. <P>Very handy for checking for intake restrictions. A friend discovered that on the 3.4L DOHC, it would create a vacuum at WOT. The water trap seemed to be the big issue. The DOHC inhales about 170-180 gms.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 05-17-2001).]||||reg||1
